# snapshot.json

What `jira-flow-report collect` writes and `aggregate.py` reads. Produce this
shape by any route — the Jira REST API, an MCP connector, a CSV export you
reshape — and steps 2 and 3 work unchanged.

```json
{
  "schema": 1,
  "server":  "${server}",
  "project": "${project}",
  "board":   ${board_json},
  "jql":     "<the query used>",
  "labels":  ${labels_json},
  "stages":  ${stages_json},
  "parked":  "${parked}",
  "track":   ${track_json},
  "done":    "${done}",
  "status_aliases": ${aliases_json},
  "issues": [
    {
      "key":      "${sample_key}",
      "summary":  "<one line>",
      "labels":   ${sample_labels},
      "status":   "${done}",
      "assignee": "<username or null>",
      "created":  "2026-01-31T10:14:22.000+0000",
      "history": [
        {"at": "2026-02-01T09:02:11.000+0000", "by": "<username>",
         "from": "${parked}", "to": "<next status>"}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Field notes:

- `status` — the **current** status, spelled the way the REST fields spell it
  (which may be localised).
- `history` — **only** `status` changelog items, ascending by `at`. Other field
  changes are dropped at collect time. `from`/`to` are spelled the way the
  changelog spells them, which may differ from the field spelling;
  `status_aliases` maps one onto the other.
- `status_aliases` — `{"<changelog spelling>": "<field spelling>"}`. Only
  genuinely differing pairs are listed; anything absent is used as-is. Discovered
  at collect time, never hardcoded.
- `stages` / `parked` / `track` / `done` — the stage scale and its roles, so the
  offline steps need no config file. CLI flags override them.
- `history` may be empty: an issue created straight into a status and never moved.
  `aggregate.py` then falls back to `created` for the parked-since date.
- `assignee` — the username as your Jira spells it (Jira Server uses `name`,
  Jira Cloud an account id), or `null` for unassigned.
- `at` and `created` — only the first 10 characters are read, so any ISO-8601
  form works and the timezone is ignored. A transition just after midnight lands
  on the date its string carries.
- `labels` keeps the original case; folding happens during aggregation.

Minimum viable issue record: `key`, `summary`, `labels`, `status`, `assignee`,
`created`, `history`. Anything else in the object is ignored.
